ation  of a battle of britain command room to  show you exactly how data was  disseminated and acted on quickly to  allow british pilots to intercept german  planes within minutes have been notified  of their approach  this isn't like the same old boring  history documentaries being remade over  and over again these days repeating  themselves constantly for their 30  minute run times so they can fit enough  ads in this episode goes over a mock  raid from german planes showing how  information was quickly filtered  ratified and displayed on a massive map  of britain to allow british pilots to  quickly receive orders in an age before  digital data processing existed this is  the nitty gritty detail that you have  come to enjoy from real engineering just  applied to a different genre  we have made nebula the home of our  world war ii series as historically our  videos on these subjects are often  demonetized and suppressed on youtube  something we've tried to tiptoe around  in this video by avoiding certain words  by signing up you'll get access to our  9-part series on the logistics of d-day  this ongoing battle of britain series as  well as real-life loris monthly modern  conflict series where he explores modern  conflicts like his last two episodes on  the russian invasions of chechnya and  georgia on top of all that you get  access to curiositystream's massive  library of award-winning documentaries  you can get all of that for the low  price of 14.79 a year  and we will be donating five dollars for  every person that signs up to nebula in  the next month to aid ukrainian refugees  fleeing the conflict on average one  thousand people sign up with my link  every month so i am preemptively  donating five thousand dollars today  i've posted proof of that donation on my  instagram account and on the community  page here if you are looking for  something else to watch right now you  can watch our last video on the  uncertain future of international  cooperation for the 